&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About ClickHouse&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized on the 2025 Forbes Cloud 100 list, ClickHouse is one of the most innovative and fast-growing private cloud companies. With more than 4,000 customers and ARR that has grown over 250 percent year over year, ClickHouse leads the market in real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s sustained, accelerating momentum was recently validated by a $400M Series D financing round. Over the past three months, customers including Capital One, Lovable, Decagon, Polymarket, and Airwallex have adopted the platform or expanded existing deployments. These customers join an established base of AI innovators and global brands such as Meta, Cursor, Sony, and Tesla.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to transform how companies use data. Come be a part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Director of Product Management to own our security product strategy end to end - &amp;nbsp; the vision, the roadmap, build vs buy decisions. You will set the multi-year investment strategy for our security offerings, go deep with engineering on database security, networking, and identity management. You will be the subject matter expert for other PMs navigating security-adjacent decisions..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, strategy, and multi-year roadmap for our security offerings, and make the case for it - internally with engineering and leadership, and externally with customers and the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go deep on database security, networking, and identity and access management (IAM) - enough to argue the details with engineering, not just approve what they propose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, design, sales, and marketing to ship products that are actually secure, not just marketed that way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex security requirements into specifications and user stories that engineering can understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own backlog prioritization and the trade-offs that come with it, weighing business value, customer risk, and engineering cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive go-to-market for security launches - positioning, sales enablement, documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor how security features perform in the real world and use that data, not just instinct, to decide what to build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the security subject-matter expert other teams come to, and provide guidance and coaching to PMs working on security-adjacent problems elsewhere in the org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent our security posture and roadmap externally - with top customers, prospects, and analysts when the conversation needs someone who actually understands the tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management experience in B2B SaaS, with a significant and sustained focus on security products or features, including experience setting security strategy at an organizational level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real, hands-on experience with database security principles and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking concepts and their security implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of identity and access management (IAM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISM, CompTIA Security+) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid program management skills: planning, execution, and risk management across multiple concurrent workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of representing product externally - with customers, analysts, or at industry events, and translating deep technical security topics for non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding or informally mentoring other PMs, even without a formal reporting relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills, and the judgment to know when to escalate versus when to just make the call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a fast-paced, collaborative environment where priorities shift and you&#39;re expected to bring order to it, not just follow along.&lt;/li&gt;
