&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About ClickHouse&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized on the 2025 Forbes Cloud 100 list, ClickHouse is one of the most innovative and fast-growing private cloud companies. With more than 4,000 customers and ARR that has grown over 250 percent year over year, ClickHouse leads the market in real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s sustained, accelerating momentum was recently validated by a $400M Series D financing round. Over the past three months, customers including Capital One, Lovable, Decagon, Polymarket, and Airwallex have adopted the platform or expanded existing deployments. These customers join an established base of AI innovators and global brands such as Meta, Cursor, Sony, and Tesla.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to transform how companies use data. Come be a part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As ClickHouse moves further into &lt;strong&gt;financial services, healthcare, telco, and the public sector&lt;/strong&gt; across EMEA, more of our deals now turn on a specific set of questions: where the data lives, who can reach it, how it&#39;s encrypted, and what the auditor needs to see. We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Security Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to own those conversations, a &lt;strong&gt;specialist overlay within our EMEA Solutions Architecture team&lt;/strong&gt;, brought in when security, data residency, or regulatory compliance conversations come up on a deal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ideal candidate comes from &lt;strong&gt;inside the data industry&lt;/strong&gt; - and pairs &lt;strong&gt;deep security expertise with real data architecture depth&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll be the credible technical voice in front of CISOs and security architects, and the internal authority our field relies on for answers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the &lt;strong&gt;security overlay on EMEA opportunities&lt;/strong&gt; supporting conversations related to security, privacy, or compliance, engaging customers and prospects alongside the account Solutions Architect and Account Executive, discussing our various deployment models, BYOC architectures and all related security questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead security conversations with &lt;strong&gt;CISOs, security architects, and GRC teams&lt;/strong&gt;, translating ClickHouse architecture into the controls frameworks they recognize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and validate &lt;strong&gt;secure ClickHouse Cloud and BYOC deployment patterns&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; network isolation, private connectivity, encryption, customer-managed keys, identity federation, and granular access control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;strong&gt;threat modelling and architecture reviews&lt;/strong&gt; with customer security teams, and own the security workstream through POC and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the field&#39;s authority on our compliance posture — &lt;strong&gt;SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, GDPR and EU data residency, HIPAA, PCI DSS&lt;/strong&gt;, and the European regulatory picture including DORA and NIS2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the quality and speed of &lt;strong&gt;security questionnaires, RFP security sections, DPIAs, and third-party risk reviews&lt;/strong&gt;, building the reusable answer library as you go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the &lt;strong&gt;security playbook for EMEA Solutions Architecture&lt;/strong&gt; and enable SAs and AEs so routine security questions stay with the account team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant customer-facing technical experience at a &lt;strong&gt;data platform, analytics, streaming, or database company&lt;/strong&gt; — you understand data architecture, not just security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable depth in &lt;strong&gt;cloud and data security&lt;/strong&gt;: IAM, key management and cryptography, network isolation, secure multi-tenancy, threat modelling, and audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working command of the frameworks that gate enterprise data deals — &lt;strong&gt;SOC 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HIPAA, PCI DSS&lt;/strong&gt; — and comfort with EU regulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Credibility with security buyers.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve held your own in front of a CISO and know the difference between answering the question and getting through the meeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overlay instincts&lt;/strong&gt; and clear writing — comfortable working through others, prioritizing across a region, and producing artefacts that survive an auditor&#39;s reading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security certifications such as &lt;strong&gt;CISSP, CCSP, or CISM&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on security architecture experience across &lt;strong&gt;AWS, GCP, and Azure&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in &lt;strong&gt;regulated industries&lt;/strong&gt; — financial services, healthcare, telco, or the public sector.&lt;/li&gt;
