&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About ClickHouse&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized on the 2025 Forbes Cloud 100 list, ClickHouse is one of the most innovative and fast-growing private cloud companies. With more than 4,000 customers and ARR that has grown over 250 percent year over year, ClickHouse leads the market in real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s sustained, accelerating momentum was recently validated by a $400M Series D financing round. Over the past three months, customers including Capital One, Lovable, Decagon, Polymarket, and Airwallex have adopted the platform or expanded existing deployments. These customers join an established base of AI innovators and global brands such as Meta, Cursor, Sony, and Tesla.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to transform how companies use data. Come be a part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Solutions Architect to serve as the primary technical partner for our prospects and customers. You&#39;ll work hand-in-hand with Sales throughout the full lifecycle: qualifying technical requirements, designing and proving out architectures, running proofs of concept, and guiding customers from first evaluation through to production at scale. You&#39;ll be the trusted technical voice in the room, translating ClickHouse&#39;s architecture and capabilities into solutions that solve real business problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical advisor for prospects and customers evaluating or scaling ClickHouse, from discovery through production deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design reference architectures, data models, and ingestion/query patterns tailored to each customer&#39;s use case, scale, and existing data stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and run technical proofs of concept and benchmarks, demonstrating ClickHouse&#39;s performance, scalability, and cost advantages against incumbent solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Account Executives to build technical account strategy, navigate procurement/security reviews, and close complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling technical presentations, demos, and workshops to audiences ranging from individual engineers to VP/C-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise customers on schema design, query optimization, cluster sizing, replication, and migration strategy from other databases (e.g., Postgres, Elasticsearch, Snowflake, Druid, Spark).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer internally, feeding product and engineering teams structured feedback on gaps, feature requests, and competitive positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable assets, demos, and technical content (blog posts, reference architectures, sample apps) that scale your impact across the field team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team best practices, tooling, and onboarding materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a customer-facing technical role such as Solutions Architect, Sales Engineer, Data Engineer, or Technical Consultant, ideally at an infrastructure, database, or analytics company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with SQL and analytical/OLAP databases (ClickHouse, Snowflake, BigQuery, Druid, Vertica, Redshift, or similar); ClickHouse experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of distributed systems fundamentals: partitioning, replication, consistency trade-offs, and query execution at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across the modern data stack, including streaming systems (Kafka), orchestration tools, BI tools, and cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, or Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to run and win technical evaluations against competitive alternatives, with a track record of influencing buying decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, able to flex between whiteboarding with engineers and presenting business value to executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who thrives with ambiguity and enjoys being both hands-on with technology and directly responsible for revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel periodically for customer visits, conferences, and team events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience deploying or administering ClickHouse in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time analytics, observability, or large-scale event/log data use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source data infrastructure projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at an early-stage or hypergrowth startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
