&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to transform how companies use data. Come be a part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Finance Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team and serve as a strategic partner to Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market organizations. This is a high-impact, cross-functional role which touches the full ClickHouse P&amp;amp;L. You will bring strong analytical skills and business acumen to drive data-driven financial decision making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director of Product Finance, you will have visibility to the Executive team and play a meaningful role in shaping how ClickHouse thinks about growth, pricing, and resource allocation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic partner from Finance to Product, Engineering, and GTM functions, bringing analytical backing to support business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model the financial impact of strategic initiatives across the business. Perform analysis to support investment decisions, new product launches, efficiency projects, pricing strategy, and go-to-market design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze KPIs across both Product and GTM to drive improvement across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual planning and monthly forecast and variance review cycles. Partner with Product, Engineering, and GTM leadership to accurately forecast the business, and measure performance against these forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Accounting to ensure accuracy in revenue recognition, commissions, and expense allocation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize financial results and KPIs for executive and board reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Bring Along&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–6 years of experience in a data-heavy analytical role, FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, investment banking, or management consulting, ideally with exposure to SaaS or consumption-based business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intrinsic motivation to take on challenging problems and a bias toward action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data skills. SQL fluency is a must; Python experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial modeling capabilities in Excel and/or Google Sheets; able to build dynamic, driver-based models independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with large datasets and translating analytical outputs into clear business insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills; ability to distill complexity for senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of accounting principles, with an understanding of how financial data flows through revenue recognition, commissions, and expense processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools and a willingness to leverage them in day-to-day work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Data Science, Finance, Economics, Business, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with financial planning and BI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The typical starting salary for this role in the US is&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$135,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The typical starting salary for this role in US Premium Markets is&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
